WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.968
-Guys, it is time for "Tonight
Show" Hashtags. Here we go.

00:00:03.968 --> 00:00:05.634
♪ -Hashtags ♪

00:00:05.634 --> 00:00:08.234
♪♪

00:00:08.234 --> 00:00:10.033
♪ Hashtags ♪

00:00:10.033 --> 00:00:13.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.434 --> 00:00:17.100
-Well, we do this thing every
week where I send out a hashtag

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.567
and I ask you guys
to respond to that topic.

00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:22.367
So with the infrastructure bill
recently passing,

00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:24.934
I sent out the hashtag
#TheyNeedToFix.

00:00:24.934 --> 00:00:27.634
And I asked you guys to share
a weird or funny problem

00:00:27.634 --> 00:00:29.033
that needs a solution.

00:00:29.033 --> 00:00:30.934
Yeah. Within minutes,
it was a trending topic,

00:00:30.934 --> 00:00:32.300
so thank you for playing along.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:33.501
And now I thought I'd share

00:00:33.501 --> 00:00:35.334
some of my favorite responses
from you guys.

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:36.467
Here we go.

00:00:36.467 --> 00:00:39.601
This first one is
from @kansasbradbury.

00:00:39.601 --> 00:00:42.300
He says,
"They need to fix it so food

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:43.934
has three different
expiration dates --

00:00:43.934 --> 00:00:46.300
one date that says 'Best
before,' then one called

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:49.334
'still pretty good' and finally,
'Are you feeling lucky?'"

00:00:49.334 --> 00:00:50.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:50.701 --> 00:00:52.467
I like that.
-I love it.

00:00:52.467 --> 00:00:54.767
-Beats the sniff test.

00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:56.634
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:56.634 --> 00:01:00.501
This one's from @ahnah96.
-Ahnah?

00:01:00.501 --> 00:01:01.934
-Ah, nah.
-Ah.

00:01:01.934 --> 00:01:03.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.868 --> 00:01:06.868
-Could be Anna.
-What does she say?

00:01:06.868 --> 00:01:10.267
-She says, "They need to fix
how they package scissors.

00:01:10.267 --> 00:01:11.901
To remove the packaging,
you need scissors.

00:01:11.901 --> 00:01:13.634
If I had a pair of scissors
in the first place,

00:01:13.634 --> 00:01:15.067
I wouldn't need to buy
another one."

00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:18.167
[ Applause ]

00:01:18.167 --> 00:01:21.334
"Honey, get me
the scissor-opening scissors."

00:01:21.334 --> 00:01:24.400
This is from @bakeross1988.

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:26.234
He says, "They need to fix songs
that have

00:01:26.234 --> 00:01:28.133
police or ambulance sirens
in them,

00:01:28.133 --> 00:01:29.601
so when you're listening to them
in a car,

00:01:29.601 --> 00:01:31.901
a voice says, 'This is not real.
Do not pull over.'"

00:01:31.901 --> 00:01:32.968
[ Laughter ]
Yes! I agree with that!

00:01:32.968 --> 00:01:34.901
-Yes!

00:01:34.901 --> 00:01:38.534
I totally agree with that.

00:01:38.534 --> 00:01:40.467
This one is from
@dundermifflin84.

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:41.934
-Oh, wow.

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:44.634
-He says, "They need to fix beer
prices at sports games.

00:01:44.634 --> 00:01:46.434
$10 is unacceptable.

00:01:46.434 --> 00:01:47.868
Unless I've already
had three beers,

00:01:47.868 --> 00:01:49.434
then $10 is
perfectly acceptable."

00:01:49.434 --> 00:01:52.834
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:52.834 --> 00:01:55.300
I love that.

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:58.100
This is from @breesweetack.

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:01.534
She says, "Our phones are
powerful, tiny computers

00:02:01.534 --> 00:02:04.100
that can fit in our pocket,
but vending machines still can't

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:05.934
recognize a dollar bill
with a crease in it?"

00:02:05.934 --> 00:02:10.767
[ Laughter and applause ]
Fix it!

00:02:10.767 --> 00:02:13.501
This one is from
@onufreyonboard.

00:02:13.501 --> 00:02:16.133
He says, "They need to fix
restrooms in movie theaters

00:02:16.133 --> 00:02:18.634
so that there are restrooms
in each theater with screens

00:02:18.634 --> 00:02:20.634
showing the movie,
so if you need to go,

00:02:20.634 --> 00:02:22.200
you don't miss anything."
-Ooh.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:23.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:23.634 --> 00:02:25.234
Nice.
-Wow.

00:02:25.234 --> 00:02:27.300
-Yeah.
-Really?

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:29.367
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:29.367 --> 00:02:31.033
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:02:31.033 --> 00:02:33.033
-Oh, I say absolutely not.
-What?

00:02:33.033 --> 00:02:35.100
I always go to the bathroom
at the part

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:36.634
that is the crux
of the whole movie.

00:02:36.634 --> 00:02:38.868
-I know, but you never leave
the theater.

00:02:38.868 --> 00:02:40.267
-Well, no, but I go to
the bathroom.

00:02:40.267 --> 00:02:41.767
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.767 --> 00:02:43.701
-You got those astronaut...?
-I got the astronaut diapers.

00:02:43.701 --> 00:02:46.067
Made a big splashdown.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.067 --> 00:02:49.934
-This one is from @carlsochill1.
-Ah.

00:02:49.934 --> 00:02:51.934
-He says, "They need to make
pizza boxes that can actually

00:02:51.934 --> 00:02:53.501
fit inside a refrigerator.

00:02:53.501 --> 00:02:55.534
Takes up the entire space
just for one slice

00:02:55.534 --> 00:02:56.901
that I'm going to eat
at 2:00 a.m."

00:02:56.901 --> 00:02:58.667
That's right.
[ Applause ]

00:02:58.667 --> 00:03:02.434
Come on.

00:03:02.434 --> 00:03:04.367
This last one is
from @lotsofmiles.

00:03:04.367 --> 00:03:06.434
He says, "They need to fix
cereal bags.

00:03:06.434 --> 00:03:07.968
Please. Talk to Ziploc."

00:03:07.968 --> 00:03:09.501
-Oh!
-There you have it, everybody.

00:03:09.501 --> 00:03:11.167
Those are our
"Tonight Show" hashtags.

00:03:11.167 --> 00:03:12.267
To check out
more of our favorites,

00:03:12.267 --> 00:03:14.467
go to tonightshow.com/hashtags.

